{
  "requirement": "`habeas_sdk::procedure` MUST expose:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct AgentInput<'i, D: Graph> {\n    pub node: &'i D::NodeId,\n    pub contents: &'i D::NodeContent,\n}\n\npub trait AgentInputRenderer<D: Graph>: Send + Sync {\n    fn render(&self, input: &AgentInput<'_, D>) -> Result<String, D::Error>;\n}\n```\n\nThe application MUST supply an `AgentInputRenderer<D>` through agent context\nconfiguration. Rendering MUST use the supplied contents without fetching\nreplacement contents. The SDK MUST report rendering errors as\n`ValidationError::Graph` and MUST NOT impose serialization or display bounds on\n`Graph::NodeContent` or `Graph::NodeId`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The marked tests cover each obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`.\n\n- **Exposed types and renderer supplied through context.**\n  - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs` and `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs` import `AgentInput` and `AgentInputRenderer` from `habeas_sdk::procedure`.\n  - Both implement the trait with the required `render` signature. They read `input.contents`, and `DistinctPages` in `agent.rs` also reads `input.node`.\n  - Both pass the renderer to `ValidationContext::with_agent(..., &renderer)`.\n  - A test confirms the rendered text reaches the agent: `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` asserts that the chat history contains \"source\".\n  - `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` asserts that the request contents arrive in the expected order.\n- **Rendering uses the supplied contents and does not fetch replacements.**\n  - `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` asserts that `graph.state.reads == [1, 3, 2, 3, 1]`. That is exactly one read per queued insertion, so rendering did no extra fetch.\n  - The dependency fingerprints match the rendered snapshot contents.\n- **Rendering errors surface as `ValidationError::Graph`.**\n  - `queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation` uses `FailingRenderer`, which returns `Err(\"render\")`. The test asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"render\"))`.\n  - It also asserts that no dependencies are recorded and that no agent request was made.\n- **No serialization or display bounds on `NodeContent` or `NodeId`.**\n  - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs` defines `Node` and `Contents` with, per its comment, no Serde or Hash implementations. The test compiles and runs through the whole ask/render/fingerprint path with them.\n  - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/contracts.rs` also defines application types without Hash, Serde or Display bounds.\n- **`src/authoring/sdk.rs` test.** `authoring_keeps_the_prepared_subject_snapshot_and_concrete_version` is also marked as a test of this requirement. It adds integration coverage but is not needed for adequacy.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "5197c5690b5ff5c0b3b69c76b68492d9c104108d099bfbcb31b3d48a16b78b82",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering",
